39071,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P1_ZeroShot,0,1,"The PR addresses a significant memory leak issue in AzureChatOpenAI by reusing an `httpx.AsyncClient` across instances with identical configurations. This change improves performance and resource management, which are critical for applications that may create multiple instances of this class. The addition of a test case to verify the client caching logic further ensures the correctness of the fix.",MERGE,3.56
39071,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P2_FewShot,0,1,"The PR introduces a significant improvement by caching `httpx.AsyncClient` instances based on configuration, which helps in reducing memory leaks and connection pool exhaustion. The addition of tests to verify this behavior further strengthens the PR. The code changes are well-motivated and address a known issue.",MERGE,3.09
39071,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P3_ChainOfThought,0,1,"The PR aims to fix a memory leak issue in AzureChatOpenAI by reusing an `httpx.AsyncClient` across instances with identical configurations. This is done by caching the client based on a configuration hash, which mirrors the existing caching pattern used by ChatOpenAI.",MERGE,2.87
39071,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P4_RoleBased,0,1,"The PR addresses a significant memory leak issue in the AzureChatOpenAI class by reusing an `httpx.AsyncClient` across instances with identical configurations. This change improves performance and resource management, especially when dealing with multiple instances.",MERGE,2.65
39071,C3_Diff_Commit,P1_ZeroShot,0,1,The PR addresses a significant issue with memory leaks and connection pool exhaustion in AzureChatOpenAI instances by reusing an httpx client across instances based on configuration hash. This is a performance improvement that should be beneficial for users of the service.,MERGE,2.6
39071,C3_Diff_Commit,P2_FewShot,0,1,The PR is likely to be MERGED.,MERGE,1.3
39071,C3_Diff_Commit,P3_ChainOfThought,0,1,"The PR is fixing an issue where AzureChatOpenAI was creating a new httpx.AsyncClient on each instantiation, leading to memory leaks and connection pool exhaustion when many LLM instances are created. The fix involves caching the root client based on configuration hash so identical configurations reuse the same client.",MERGE,3.04
39071,C3_Diff_Commit,P4_RoleBased,0,1,"The commit message clearly describes the problem and the solution, which is to reuse an httpx client across AzureChatOpenAI instances based on configuration hash. This change addresses memory leaks and connection pool exhaustion issues when many LLM instances are created.",MERGE,2.67
39071,C4_Full_Context,P1_ZeroShot,0,1,"The PR addresses a significant issue with memory leaks and connection pool exhaustion in AzureChatOpenAI instances by caching the `httpx.AsyncClient` based on configuration hash. This fix improves performance and resource management, aligning with best practices for client reuse in network-based applications. The addition of unit tests ensures that the caching logic works as expected without breaking existing functionality.",MERGE,3.75
39071,C4_Full_Context,P2_FewShot,0,1,"The PR introduces a significant improvement by caching the `httpx.AsyncClient` across multiple instances of `AzureChatOpenAI`, which can help prevent memory leaks and connection pool exhaustion. The addition of a test case to verify this behavior is also a positive aspect. The code changes are well-motivated and address a real problem.",MERGE,3.36
39071,C4_Full_Context,P3_ChainOfThought,0,1,The PR addresses a memory leak issue in AzureChatOpenAI by reusing an httpx.AsyncClient across instances with identical configurations. This change is necessary to prevent connection pool exhaustion when many LLM instances are created.,MERGE,2.5
