123906,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P1_ZeroShot,1,1,"The PR introduces a new frontend attribute `collective_group_key` to control how collectives are combined, which can help in organizing and scheduling collectives more effectively. The changes include adding helpers for handling this attribute, modifying combining boundaries, and ensuring that the key is correctly propagated through various rewrites. These modifications seem well-thought-out and address a specific need in XLA's functionality.",MERGE,4.95
123906,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P2_FewShot,1,1,"The PR introduces a new feature that adds a `collective_group_key` frontend attribute to XLA, which allows grouping different collectives together as a group. This feature is motivated by the need to stop XLA from combining collectives from unrelated layers and instead allow grouping different collectives together as a group. The changes include adding the attribute contract, handling combining boundaries, key forwarding through non-combining rewrites, and updating various collective operations to use this new attribute. The PR also includes documentation for the new attribute semantics.",MERGE,6.27
