326665,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P1_ZeroShot,1,1,"The PR introduces a feature that suggests users disable an extension when a built-in alternative is available, which can improve user experience and reduce resource usage. The implementation includes a one-time notification mechanism to ensure the prompt is shown only once per application session. The code appears well-structured and follows best practices for VS Code development.",MERGE,9.63
326665,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P2_FewShot,1,1,"The PR introduces a new feature that provides a one-time notification to users about disabling an extension when built-in dictation is available. The implementation includes checks for platform support, built-in dictation enabled status, extension installation and enablement, and ensures the prompt is shown only once. The code changes are well-documented, and the testing section confirms that the feature works as expected.",MERGE,10.87
326665,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P3_ChainOfThought,1,1,The PR introduces a new feature to prompt users to disable the 'VS Code Speech' extension when built-in dictation is available in VS Code. The changes include adding a new workbench contribution `RedundantDictationExtensionNotifier` that shows a one-time notification under specific conditions.,MERGE,8.16
326665,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P4_RoleBased,1,1,"The PR introduces a feature to notify users about disabling the redundant 'VS Code Speech' extension when built-in dictation is available. The implementation includes a new workbench contribution `RedundantDictationExtensionNotifier` that checks for platform support, built-in dictation enabled status, and the presence of the extension before showing the notification. The notification also ensures it does not reappear after being shown once.",MERGE,11.64
