327482,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P1_ZeroShot,0,1,"The PR addresses a significant issue where image attachments in the Agents window were not being properly resolved to bytes, causing the model to perceive them as uri-only references rather than actual images. The fix introduces a new `IFileService` for reading referenced files and emitting `EmbeddedResource` with base64 data, which resolves the problem. The PR also includes regression tests to ensure that the fix works as expected.",MERGE,4.81
327482,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P2_FewShot,0,1,"The PR introduces a defensive check against None values, which is a good practice and aligns with best coding standards. The changes are well-documented, and the tests cover various scenarios, ensuring that the functionality works as expected. The code review feedback provided is positive and indicates that the changes are ready to be merged.",MERGE,4.19
327482,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P3_ChainOfThought,0,1,"The PR aims to improve image handling in the Agents window by ensuring that images are sent as embedded bytes to the model, rather than just a URI reference. This change addresses issues related to image perception by the model and improves the overall user experience.",MERGE,3.0
327482,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P4_RoleBased,0,1,"The PR addresses an important issue where image attachments in the Agents window were not being properly resolved to bytes, causing them to be perceived incorrectly by the model. The fix introduces a new `IFileService` for reading file contents and converting them to base64-encoded data, which is then embedded in the message attachment. This ensures that the model receives the actual image data rather than just a path reference.",MERGE,10.12
327482,C3_Diff_Commit,P1_ZeroShot,0,1,"The PR introduces changes to handle image attachments more efficiently by sending them as embedded bytes instead of resource paths, which should improve the functionality and user experience for Copilot and Codex. The addition of a regression test ensures that non-hydrating draft image attachments are handled correctly, which is an important aspect of maintaining the system's stability. The changes are well-documented with commit messages and co-authored by the Copilot App, indicating thorough testing and collaboration.",MERGE,12.71
327482,C3_Diff_Commit,P2_FewShot,0,1,"The PR contains two commits with different purposes and impacts. The first commit adds a defensive check against None values, which is generally a good practice and can improve the robustness of the code. However, the second commit introduces changes to how image attachments are handled in drafts, which includes making certain operations asynchronous and adding regression tests. These changes are more substantial and could potentially introduce new issues if not thoroughly tested. The PR also mentions follow-up work for other issues, indicating that it is part of a larger effort.",MERGE,13.3
327482,C3_Diff_Commit,P3_ChainOfThought,0,1,"The PR includes two commits that address issues related to image attachments in a chat draft. The first commit modifies the way image attachments are handled, ensuring that they are sent as embedded bytes instead of resource paths when possible. This change is intended to improve the functionality of Copilot and Codex, although it does not affect Claude. The second commit adds a regression test for non-hydrating draft image attachments, which ensures that the behavior remains consistent with previous versions.",MERGE,11.99
327482,C3_Diff_Commit,P4_RoleBased,0,1,"The commit messages provide clear context for the changes made in the code, explaining why certain modifications were necessary and how they address existing issues. The code diff shows that the changes are focused on handling image attachments more efficiently by sending them as embedded bytes instead of resource paths, which should improve the functionality of the Agents window agent. Additionally, a regression test has been added to ensure that non-hydrating draft image attachments behave as expected.",MERGE,11.93
327482,C4_Full_Context,P1_ZeroShot,0,1,"The PR introduces a significant change to how image attachments are handled in the Agents window, ensuring that images are sent as embedded bytes rather than just URI references. This is crucial for improving model perception and user experience. The changes include adding an `IFileService` for reading file bytes, handling potential read failures gracefully, and ensuring that draft input-state syncs remain lightweight. The PR also includes comprehensive regression tests to validate the functionality. Given the importance of this change and the thorough testing provided, it is highly likely that the PR will be merged.",MERGE,14.37
327482,C4_Full_Context,P2_FewShot,0,1,"The PR introduces a significant improvement by ensuring that image attachments are properly hydrated and sent to the model as embedded bytes, which addresses a critical issue in how images were previously handled. The addition of regression tests further validates the changes and ensures that the existing functionality is not broken. The code review feedback provided is positive and acknowledges the defensive check against None values, indicating that the PR meets the necessary quality standards.",MERGE,11.37
327482,C4_Full_Context,P3_ChainOfThought,0,1,"The PR introduces a change to how image attachments are handled in the Agents window, specifically for model-facing conversions. It reads referenced files via an injected `IFileService` and emits an `EmbeddedResource` with base64 data for these conversions, falling back to the existing `MessageAttachmentKind.Resource` path reference on any read failure. The conversion caller chain is now async, and per-session pending-message syncs are serialized and coalesced through a `ThrottlerByKey`. This change helps Copilot and Codex but does not affect Claude.",MERGE,13.52
327482,C4_Full_Context,P4_RoleBased,0,1,"The PR addresses an important issue where image attachments in the Agents window were not being properly resolved to bytes, causing them to be invisible to the model. The fix introduces a new `IFileService` for reading referenced files and emitting `EmbeddedResource` with base64 data for model-facing conversions. This ensures that images are correctly sent to the agent as embedded bytes, improving the overall functionality of the system.",MERGE,11.17
