140477,C3_Diff_Commit,P3_ChainOfThought,0,1,"The PR is making a change to how pod-level resource keys are handled in PodRequests and PodLimits. Specifically, it's omitting unactuated pod-level resource keys from the effective map when building pod-level aggregation. This ensures that only actuated keys are propagated, which aligns with container-level aggregation.",MERGE,3.45
140477,C3_Diff_Commit,P4_RoleBased,0,1,The commit message clearly explains the problem and provides a detailed solution. The code diff shows that the changes are focused on ensuring consistency between pod-level and container-level aggregation by omitting unactuated keys in PodRequests/PodLimits. This is important for future work on pod-level resize GA.,MERGE,3.4
140477,C4_Full_Context,P1_ZeroShot,0,1,"The PR addresses a consistency issue in how pod-level resource aggregation is handled compared to container-level aggregation, which can lead to discrepancies in reported resource limits and requests. The fix ensures that unactuated keys are omitted from the effective maps, making the pod-level aggregation consistent with the container-level one. This change does not introduce any new behavior or observable changes for existing consumers of these resources.",MERGE,7.64
