140477,C4_Full_Context,P3_ChainOfThought,0,1,"The PR is making a change to how pod-level resource keys are handled in PodRequests and PodLimits. Specifically, it's ensuring that unactuated keys are omitted from the effective map, rather than being inserted with an explicit zero value. This change is intended to make pod-level aggregation match container-level aggregation, which is not currently observable via any in-tree cgroup/enforcement path.",MERGE,10.56
140477,C4_Full_Context,P4_RoleBased,0,1,"The PR addresses an inconsistency in how pod-level resource aggregation is handled compared to container-level aggregation, which can lead to different key sets for the same input. This inconsistency could potentially cause confusion or issues when consumers rely on consistent behavior across both levels of aggregation.",MERGE,7.82
