327325,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P1_ZeroShot,0,1,"The proposed change addresses a common issue with custom dialog titles being clipped due to verbose text. By allowing the message container and title to shrink, and constraining titles to one line with an ellipsis, the PR ensures that the titles remain readable even when they are long. This is a straightforward improvement that should enhance user experience without introducing any significant complexity or potential issues.",MERGE,9.4
327325,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P2_FewShot,0,1,"The PR introduces a CSS change to prevent custom dialog title clipping by allowing titles to shrink and using an ellipsis for overflow text. This is a defensive check against potential issues with verbose titles in dialogs, which could improve user experience. The code diff shows that the CSS changes are straightforward and do not introduce any significant complexity or risk.",MERGE,8.78
327325,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P3_ChainOfThought,0,1,"The PR is addressing an issue where verbose titles in custom dialogs could be vertically clipped instead of remaining readable. The proposed change allows the message container and title to shrink, and constrains titles to one line with an ellipsis.",MERGE,6.73
327325,C2_Diff_PR_Body,P4_RoleBased,0,1,"The proposed change addresses the issue of verbose titles in custom dialogs being vertically clipped, which can make them less readable. By allowing the message container and title to shrink and constraining titles to one line with an ellipsis, the solution ensures that all text remains visible without compromising readability.",MERGE,7.84
